  "_about": [
    "Hand-labelled expected values for eval/cases/*.txt, read off each CV by eye.",
    "",
    "`difficulty` names what each case is actually testing, so a regression can be",
    "attributed to a cause rather than just a lower number. `skills_must_include`",
    "is a recall floor on the terms a recruiter would search for -- skill",
    "extraction is partly subjective, so exact-set matching would measure",
    "agreement with my taste rather than correctness.",
    "",
    "Limitation, stated up front: these CVs are synthetic. They were written to",
    "exercise known failure modes (column interleaving, abbreviated dates,",
    "year-only ranges, tabular roles, promotions within one employer), not",
    "sampled from real applications, so the numbers describe the extractor",
    "against those failure modes and not against the true distribution of CVs."
  ],
